-- title:
--   Local extension is surjective from a cotangent condition on its completion
-- statement:
--   Let $R$, $S$ and $M$ be commutative rings, each Noetherian local, with $S$ an $R$-algebra that is finite as an $R$-module and whose structure map $R \to S$ is local (it carries non-units to non-units). Assume the residue extension is trivial in the strong form that for every $s \in S$ there is $r \in R$ with $s - \mathrm{algebraMap}_{R,S}(r) \in \mathfrak m_S$. Let $\widehat S = \mathrm{AdicCompletion}(\mathfrak m_S, S)$ be the $\mathfrak m_S$-adic completion of $S$ and let $\iota \colon \widehat S \xrightarrow{\sim} M$ be a ring isomorphism. Suppose finally that
--   $$\mathfrak m_M \;\le\; \mathfrak m_R \cdot M \;+\; \mathfrak m_M^{\,2},$$
--   where $\mathfrak m_R \cdot M$ is the ideal of $M$ generated by the image of $\mathfrak m_R$ under the composite $R \to S \to \widehat S \xrightarrow{\iota} M$. Then the structure map $\mathrm{algebraMap}_{R,S} \colon R \to S$ is surjective, so $S$ is a quotient of $R$.
--
--   This is a Nakayama-type criterion for a finite local extension with trivial residue extension to be an isomorphism onto its image, the hypothesis being imposed on an arbitrary local model $M$ of the completion rather than on $S$ itself. It is used in the study of local rings of modular curves, where it is applied to a ring isomorphism identifying the completion of a localisation of a modular curve with an explicit crossing model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsLocalRing_surjective_algebraMap_of_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_of_maximalIdeal_le_map_sup_sq.lean

